    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Use shared decision-making to select integrated evidence-based treatment for alcohol use disorder and PTSD. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023) [S]</item><item>Offer behavioral AUD treatment and discuss FDA-approved medication options; patient initially selects behavioral treatment. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); Recommend Evidence-Based Treatment: Know the Options (2026 accessed) [S]</item><item>Begin trauma-focused psychotherapy without requiring recovery to be perfect or linear. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023) [S]</item><item>Referral to behavioral health for trauma-focused psychotherapy within integrated recovery care. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023) [S]</item><item>Repeat AUDIT-C, PCL-5, and PHQ-9 at six and twelve weeks and maintain a collaborative relapse and safety plan. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
